---
const updated = '2026-05-12';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Privacy Policy | Adorable</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Adorable AB." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://adorable.se/privacy" />
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        background: #faf7f2;
        color: #171412;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 48px 20px;
      }

      main {
        max-width: 820px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        background: #fff;
        border: 1px solid rgba(23, 20, 18, 0.12);
        border-radius: 24px;
        padding: 48px;
        box-shadow: 0 24px 80px rgba(23, 20, 18, 0.08);
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 8px;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }

      h2 {
        margin-top: 36px;
        font-size: 1.2rem;
      }

      p, li {
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .muted {
        color: #6d625b;
      }

      a {
        color: #171412;
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        body {
          padding: 20px 12px;
        }

        main {
          padding: 28px;
          border-radius: 18px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Adorable AB (“Adorable”, “we”, “us” or “our”) may collect, use and protect personal data when you visit our website, contact us, use our services or interact with tools, automations, advertising platforms or integrations operated in connection with our work.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Company information</h2>
      <p>
        Adorable AB is a Swedish company registered under organisation number 559095-2122. Contact: <a href="mailto:peter@adorable.se">peter@adorable.se</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to our website and general business operations. Client-specific data processing may be governed by separate agreements, data processing agreements, platform terms, statements of work or written instructions. If a separate agreement conflicts with this general policy, the separate agreement applies to that client engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Data we may collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Contact details such as name, email address, phone number, company and role.</li>
        <li>Messages, requests, feedback and other information you choose to send to us.</li>
        <li>Business information needed to provide consulting, marketing, analytics or AI advisory services.</li>
        <li>Technical data such as IP address, browser, device, pages visited, referrer, timestamps and basic usage events.</li>
        <li>Advertising, analytics, CRM or platform data that a client chooses to provide or authorise us to access.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we use data</h2>
      <p>We may use personal data to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to enquiries and communicate with clients, prospects and partners.</li>
        <li>Provide, manage, analyse and improve our services.</li>
        <li>Run marketing, analytics, reporting, automation and AI-assisted workflows.</li>
        <li>Maintain security, prevent misuse and troubleshoot technical issues.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal, accounting, tax and administrative requirements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Legal bases</h2>
      <p>
        Where GDPR applies, we rely on appropriate legal bases, including performance of a contract, legitimate interests, consent where required, and compliance with legal obligations. Our legitimate interests may include operating our business, communicating with relevant contacts, improving services, measuring website performance and protecting systems from misuse.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Website analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We may use privacy-friendly analytics to understand website usage and improve the site. Analytics data is used in aggregate where possible. We do not use website analytics to intentionally identify individual visitors unless required for security, troubleshooting or legal reasons.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        We may use third-party services, including advertising platforms, analytics providers, hosting providers, AI providers, communication tools, automation tools and business software. These providers may process data according to their own terms, privacy policies and technical systems. We are not responsible for independent third-party platforms, outages, policy decisions, data handling, security incidents, model outputs, tracking limitations or changes made by those providers, except where mandatory law says otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Advertising and platform data</h2>
      <p>
        When working with advertising accounts, pixels, datasets, APIs, custom audiences, conversion events or campaign data, we act according to the access and instructions provided by the relevant account owner or client. The account owner remains responsible for having valid rights, notices, consents and legal bases for the data made available to us and for ensuring compliance with applicable platform policies and laws.
      </p>

      <h2>9. AI and automation</h2>
      <p>
        AI and automation systems may be used to support analysis, reporting, content drafting, data processing or operational workflows. AI-generated outputs can be inaccurate, incomplete or unsuitable. Human review is required before relying on AI outputs for publication, legal compliance, financial decisions, employment decisions or other important uses. We disclaim responsibility for how clients or third parties use AI outputs, except where mandatory law requires otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Sharing of data</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. We may share data with service providers, subcontractors, professional advisors, authorities where legally required, or platforms and tools necessary to provide our services. We only share what is reasonably necessary for the relevant purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>11. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some providers may process data outside the EU/EEA. Where required, transfers are handled using appropriate safeguards such as adequacy decisions, standard contractual clauses or provider frameworks. We cannot control all independent processing by third-party platforms used by clients or visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal data only as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, for contractual performance, legitimate business needs, accounting, security, dispute handling or legal obligations. Client-provided platform data may also be retained or deleted according to the relevant client agreement, platform settings or account-owner instructions.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal data. No system, integration, AI tool, platform, transmission or storage method is completely secure. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we do not guarantee absolute security or uninterrupted availability.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Where applicable, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to processing of your personal data, and to data portability. You may also have the right to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. To exercise rights, contact <a href="mailto:peter@adorable.se">peter@adorable.se</a>. You may also contact the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY) if you believe your data protection rights have been violated.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Limitation of responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Adorable is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, punitive or exemplary damages, including loss of profit, revenue, goodwill, data, business opportunities, platform access, expected savings or campaign performance. Our responsibility is limited to what is mandatory under applicable law and any written agreement directly governing the relevant service.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Client and user responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        Clients and users are responsible for the accuracy, legality and permissions of the data, instructions, claims, audiences, tracking, consent mechanisms, files and platform access they provide. Clients are also responsible for reviewing outputs, approving campaigns, complying with platform policies and ensuring their own privacy notices and consent flows are appropriate.
      </p>

      <h2>17. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest version will be available at this URL and applies from the date it is published.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
